  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">Recommendation ITU-T Z.151 defines the User Requirements Notation (URN) intended for the elicitation, analysis, specification and validation of requirements. URN combines modelling concepts and notations for goals (mainly for non-functional requirements and quality attributes) and scenarios (mainly for operational requirements, functional requirements and performance and architectural reasoning). The goal sub-notation is called Goal-oriented Requirements Language (GRL) and the scenario sub‑notation is called Use Case Map (UCM).</abstract>
